 ```
 
+## firing it out of the store
+
+A show is designed against the house catalog and fired out of whatever the
+magazine holds, and those are never the same on the day. Give any show command
+a magazine book and every cue draws a lot from it, oldest stock first. A cue
+whose shell has run out fires the nearest thing the book still holds, same
+calibre for preference, and the cue keeps its time on the beat by lifting on
+the stand in's own flight time. Nothing covers it, and the show is not ready.
+
+```
+portfire sheet show.pf --catalog house.csv --rig autumn.rig --magazine magazine.csv
+portfire check show.pf --catalog house.csv --rig autumn.rig --magazine magazine.csv --pull vn2405,vn2413
+```
+
+`--pull` sets lot numbers aside before the draw, which is what a recall or a
+case dropped off a tailgate means. The book itself is never written to, and
+`inventory` still counts and still fails on what the script asked for, because
+a stand in is not stock and an order list with substitutions folded into it is
+an order for the wrong shells.
+
 A worked example lives in `examples/autumn`.
 
 ## the commands
